From: SheepyLord <37598021+SheepyLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 04:07:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Let replacement textures give way under real VRAM pressure

The texture manager's budget (a percentage of the free VRAM, or a fixed size)
already follows the driver's live budget, but a fixed or high budget can hold
more than the driver lets the process keep. Under real pressure the budget is
now capped from the largest device-local heap's live numbers: within a margin
below the driver's budget (2 %, at least 256 MiB) replacement textures stop
growing, and over the budget they give back the overflow plus the margin.
While the margin is free nothing changes. A rate-limited [RTX Texture Budget]
line reports the regime, the budgets, the driver numbers and the demotions.
Pure rule in rtx_texture_budget.h with test_texture_budget_pressure.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
